# Byte-exact commits for the M3 laboratory.
#
# The M1/M2 sources carry CRLF inside their committed blobs: their SHA-256 values
# in expected-sources.sha256 were measured on those exact bytes. Any end-of-line
# normalisation performed by git (core.autocrlf=true, a global .gitattributes,
# or a checkout filter) would rewrite the blobs, and the identity gate would then
# reject the tree on the Linux runner -- fail-closed, but pointless.
#
# `-text` disables ALL end-of-line conversion for every path, so what is committed
# is byte-for-byte what the manifest describes.
* -text
